  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "John A. Squires said that the future of intellectual property cannot be discussed without AI. He also said that in fields such as AI, quantum, biotechnology, advanced materials, and semiconductors, intellectual property protection and strategic management are essential national-security functions. In 2026 remarks, he said the USPTO had opened an Emerging Technologies Office in San Francisco to advance AI use and engage with the AI industry, aiming to help U.S. companies in the federal marketplace and in exporting AI products and systems.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s2",
    "s5"
   ],
